    "Hulhumale sees weddings across a mix of settings — banquet halls, hotel lawns, rooftop venues and home courtyards — and each one changes how the tying schedule is planned. A hotel booking usually means a fixed preparation room and predictable access, while a home or courtyard function often needs the team to adapt around family rituals happening in parallel. We ask about the venue type early so the right number of artists and the right pace are set from the start, rather than guessing on the day. Peak wedding months in and around Hulhumale bring tighter artist availability, so dates during the busiest weeks benefit from earlier confirmation. Off-season and weekday bookings tend to have more flexibility on timing and can sometimes accommodate later confirmations. Either way, the core planning stays the same: confirm the property, the room being used for styling, and roughly how many people need to be ready before the first ritual or the baraat departure. Weather is a smaller factor for most Hulhumale bookings since safa tying happens indoors or under cover, but for any outdoor portrait session immediately after styling, we factor in extra time so fabric and finishing hold up under natural light.",
